        "content": "### ℹ️ Operator Guidance: Condition & Fault Separation\n> **Important:** **Drift is not a failure diagnosis.**\n> - **PSI Drift Indicator (>= 0.2):** Indicates telemetry distribution has shifted compared to the train reference baseline. It warrants calibration review, not an immediate machine shutdown.\n> - **Anomaly Decision:** The champion model's statistical inference that current feature window deviates from healthy operational boundaries.\n> - **Alert State:** The locked policy's persistent decision on consecutive anomalous windows requiring maintenance investigation.",
